                <pb facs="0964" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.5151/548: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-10-18T15:00:00-03:30">October 18, 1938—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 18—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. According to the Bank of the Republic import quotas of controlled foreign
                    exchange for the month of October have just been granted to 13 countries
                    excluding the United States. Quotas total 301,500 pounds of which 100,000 are
                    for Great Britain and 100,000 for Germany.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
